Extropians,

My curiosity was piqued by Hawk's enigmatic references to the
James Donald case.  Hawk also said he did not "wish to discuss a
current case on the list."  That's fine, but in light of some of
the subsequent postings from Perry, I do wish to discuss it.

Assuming that Perry's recitations of Donald's words are correct,
It is obvious that allegations he defamed the ExI board are
utterly without merit.  I say this for two reasons.

First, speaking as a libertarian, I can see no initiation of
force in mere words.  So that leaves fraud.  Fraud is a crime
against someone who is induced to do something (or refrain from
doing something) by the intentional statements of another.  Who
here was defrauded?

Second, speaking as a lawyer, I see nothing actionable in
Donald's statements.  That might not have been the case if Donald
had said something along the lines Perry stated (see neologism,
below) when he wrote:

    He stated that the board was involved in some unnamed
    financial fraud of large proportions, and he had no
    evidence for his (incorrect) assertion. I'd say thats
    actionable regardless of who its directed at.

But that's not even close to what he said.  The pertinent quote
from Donald is as follows:

    . . . More importantly we can reasonably draw certain
    conclusions about the honesty and financial integrity of
    the Exi board from Price's cheerfull willingness to have
    them hold the purse, and his unwillingness to have
    anyone else hold the purse.

Where is the defamation?  Perhaps it is in "certain conclusions"
which "we can reasonably draw" from the situation.  Donald,
however, leaves the drawing of such conclusions as an exercise
for the student.  It would appear that Perry, Hawk et al. chose
to see ExI in a negative light.  This seems to be more a case of
"eye of the beholder," than anything really substantive.

I make no judgments regarding the plea bargain, or the possible
violation thereof.  Insufficient facts were presented from which
an informed conclusion could be made.

My advice:  Lighten up folks.  James Donald isn't a kangaroo;
let's stop threatening him with kangaroo court.  And Perry,
