Date: Fri, 12 Nov 93 21:55:20 GMT
From: sjw@liberty.demon.co.uk (Stephen J. Whitrow)
Subject: NANO: BBC TV News feature on nanotech

It's encouraging to see nanotechnology being given prime air-time.  There
was a report on BBC TV news today (repeated several times) on work being
carried out at Cambridge University involving the STM.  Film of a STM was
included, also of some resolved pictures showing hexagonal arrangements of
atoms, and of computer simulations of material surfaces at the nanometre
level.  As an ordinary electronic pc board was shown, the narrator talked
about being able to manipulate matter at an atomic level, and pointed
(pun intended) out that the technology would enable electronics to be
miniaturised an extra 1,000 times. 

So a large number of Brits have just had an introduction to /
reminder of the scanning tunneling microscope.

Steve Whitrow                           sjw@liberty.demon.co.uk

